# pr-stats output location — OPTIONAL per-user config (read by SKILL.md Step 3).
#
# Copy this file to `output-dir.txt` (which is git-ignored) and set ONE line to the
# directory where reports should be written. The first non-comment, non-empty line wins.
# Use a full path — `~` and environment variables are NOT expanded here.
#
# With no `output-dir.txt` present, reports fall back to `~/pr-stats/`.
# A directory named explicitly in the request always overrides both.
#
# Example (uncomment and edit in your copy):
# C:/Users/you/pr-reports
